    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: when an owner is created (and read back), the response must include a `displayName` field formatted exactly as `\"LastName, FirstName\"` from the stored names.\n\nThe `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated by a MapStruct mapper, so two edits were needed:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it serializes in responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes `displayName` as `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` from the stored entity names.\n\nNo OfficeFloor endpoint wiring changed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated`/`RespondWithOwner` steps already map the stored `Owner` through `OwnerMapper`, so the derived field flows through both the POST create response and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back the test asserts against.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
